⚠️ **IMPORTANT: the shim `if` chain and `helperModules` are parallel hand-maintained lists — drift silently resurrects this exact bug**

The module list (`helperModules`, line 857) and the generated `if` chain (lines 888–897) must be kept in sync by hand. When an 8th helper is added to the array but its `if` line is forgotten (or a `varName` typo lands in one place only), the catch-all silently serves `config.js` exports for that id — precisely the silent wrong-module failure class gh-908 fixes, and nothing in CI will flag it unless someone remembers to add a pinning test.

The array is already iterated to build `helperBlocks`; generate the checks from the same loop so there is a single source of truth:

```js
var helperChecks = '';
for (var hmi = 0; hmi < helperModules.length; hmi++) {
    // ... existing read + wrap ...
    helperChecks += '      if (id.indexOf("' + helperModule.id + '") !== -1) return ' + helperModule.varName + '.exports;\n';
}
var shimFn =
    'function(id) {\n' +
    '      if (id === "./configLoader.js" || id === "./configLoader" || id.indexOf("configLoader.js") !== -1) return _cl.exports;\n' +
    '      if (id.indexOf("scm.js") !== -1) return _scm.exports;\n' +
    helperChecks +
    '      return _cm.exports;\n' +
    '    }';
```

Order is preserved (array stays dependency-ordered), the generated script is byte-identical for the current seven helpers, and adding a helper becomes a one-line change.

